{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"They are **industry conventions, not SEC safe harbors or universal legal limits**. The $0.01-per-share test and 0.5%-of-NAV test are commonly used to flag pricing/NAV errors for review; firms may apply either or both, with documented policies defining scope, aggregation, materiality, and affected transactions. Falling below a threshold does not automatically make an error harmless or eliminate obligations.\n\nCorrection is governed by applicable law and regulation, fund governing documents, service-provider agreements, exchange/clearing requirements, and the fund’s board-approved NAV-error policy and procedures. Those procedures should address recalculation, reimbursement of the fund or affected investors, escalation, disclosure, and records; responsibility depends on the error’s cause and contract. Material or recurring issues warrant prompt escalation to the administrator, adviser, and fund board/counsel."}}
